      "message": "fix(app): enter a cross hole where its own line meets the stock\n\nThe cross drill read the setup stock by its largest vertex radius, so a\nbox counted at its corner circle: a 60x60 box put the mouth at r42.4\nalthough the face is at r30 (air drilling, extra Auto pecks), and the\n#84 reach check measured depth from that over-far mouth - a 30 mm hole\nfrom the face of a 44 mm square bar read 39.1 mm and a 35 mm flute was\nfalsely refused.\n\nEach hole's mouth is now where the drill's body (a square tube of\nhalf-width d/2 about the hole's line, a superset of the round drill)\nfirst meets the stock mesh, in the spindle frame; the shank's #84\nreach is read the same way at its half-width. A round bar keeps the\ncircumscribed reading bit for bit: the mesh replaces it only when the\ncrossing stands more than raw*(1-cos(pi/16)) inside it (a flat face,\nnot a tessellated round's chords), and a tube meeting no facet falls\nback to it. rapids_clear judges a rapid along a hole's line against\nthat per-line entry; every other rapid and the kernel's hop/clearance\nplanes still stand off the circumscribed radius, so station-change\nhops clear the box corners.\n\nFixes #85\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
