    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDlhMDk1YjcyZGIzZDk3ODQzNGFlNDdlY2NhN2Y3ZmZhOTEyNjc2YmQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T19:48:49Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-07T19:48:49Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app): read a cross hole's entry at the true round, part included\n\nReview fixes for the #85 per-line entry.\n\nThe flat-face band was measured against the global raw radius, so a\nround well inside it (a stepped bar's d40 section under a d60 step, an\noff-axis cylinder stock, a round boss) was read at its chords on\ngrazing off-centre lines: the mouth inside metal and the #84 reach\nshort. Each stock facet is now read as its sagitta slab, thickened by\n(h/2) tan(theta/2) from the dihedral to its edge neighbours; dihedrals\nabove 45 degrees are real edges, so box faces and hex flats stay exact\nand a round bar's chain is bit for bit (fingerprint re-checked on the\npre-#85 parent).\n\nThe per-line entry also reads the part's facets beside the stock's, so\na part poking out of a box face still bounds the mouth and the\nalong-line rapids. The refusal message regains its line continuations,\ncross_entry is a plain module of operation, and the shank branch of the\nalong-line proof is pinned on box stock.\n\nRefs #85\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
